    <bpmn:process id="W_W5332" name="W5332. In-Period Equipment Monitoring, Telematics Tracking &amp; Misuse Detection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Unit is out on rental (post W5330)
Frequency: Continuous while rented
Volume: ~40–90 units out at any time (at 3–7-day average rentals on the ~3,000–6,000 rentals/year volume)
Owner: Rental Fleet Manager
Participants: IT/IoT Engineer, HSE Officer, Customer
Source: workflow W5332 — In-Period Equipment Monitoring, Telematics Tracking &amp; Misuse Detection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5332_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5332_Lane1" name="Rental Fleet Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5332_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5332_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5332_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5332_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5332_Lane2" name="IT">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5332_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5332_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5332_Start4" name="Unit is out on rental (post W5330)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5332_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5332_Task5" name="Monitor telematics feed: location vs. agreed jobsite geofence, hour-meter…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Monitor telematics feed: location vs. agreed jobsite geofence, hour-meter accumulation, and idle/duty patterns.
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5332_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5332_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5332_Task6" name="Alert on anomalies: geofence breach (unit leaving the agreed area), excessive…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Alert on anomalies: geofence breach (unit leaving the agreed area), excessive hours vs. booked period, or kill-switch/ignition tamper.
Responsible (R): IT/IoT Engineer
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: real-time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5332_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5332_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5332_Task7" name="Triage alerts: contact renter for legitimate job-site moves vs. escalate to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Triage alerts: contact renter for legitimate job-site moves vs. escalate to recovery (W5336) for a suspected theft/breach.
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: per alert</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5332_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5332_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5332_Task8" name="Reconcile accumulated hours to the booked period; flag likely overage →…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Reconcile accumulated hours to the booked period; flag likely overage → extension billing (W5333).
Responsible (R): Rental Fleet Manager
Accountable (A): Rental Fleet Manager
Duration: daily</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5332_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5332_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5332_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5332_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
